// Testing/IndentedReport.maxon — the ONE indented list every self-check's report is assembled from.
//
// ⚠ **`panic` TAKES A STRING LITERAL** — a `let`-bound String is rejected outright — so a gate that
// found SEVERAL problems cannot hand a builder to `panic`. It has to render the list as text and
// INTERPOLATE it into the literal, which is why every check in this directory that reports all its
// failures together ends the same way.
//
// ⭐ **AND EACH OF THEM HAD WRITTEN THE LOOP ITSELF.** `LadderIndex.nameListClause`,
// `HarnessSelfTest.brokenRefusalReport`, `ScaleHistory.cellDifferenceReport` and
// `ScaleHistorySelfTest`'s two lists were four copies of one four-line builder, in four files, each of
// them file-private, with nothing that would make them agree — this project's signature bug wearing the
// costume of a formatting detail. They agreed today; a change to how a list is rendered would have
// reached one of them and read as deliberate at the other three.
//
// THE INDENT STAYS THE CALLER'S, and that is not an escape hatch. How deep a list sits is a property of
// the SENTENCE that introduces it — a fixture under a headline, a missing expectation under the fixture
// that is missing it, a differing cell under the row it was read from — and folding those depths in here
// would be one constant standing for three different nestings.
export function indentedList(items StringArray, indent String) returns String
	var out = StringBuilder.create()
	for item in items 'eachItem'
		out.append("{indent}{item}")
	end 'eachItem'
	return out.build()
end 'indentedList'
